<!-- 01 — THE SITUATION -->
<section class="container measure section-block section-block--tight">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">01 — The situation</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Hundreds of applications, one cut-off date</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">A new brand presence is decided once and applied a thousand times: on signs and vehicles, on products and packaging, in presentations, forms, signatures, on the website and in every video. If this is not rolled out in an orderly way, the old lives on next to the new for a long time.</p>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Customers then see two senders — and wonder which one counts. Exactly what the decision was meant to end.</p>
  <p class="pull-quote reveal reveal-delay-2">A brand presence that is consistent only in the manual is not consistent.</p>
</section>

<!-- 02 — WHAT IS CREATED -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">02 — What is created</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">From the logo to every application</h2>
  <ul class="check-list">
    {%- for item in [
      "An inventory of all applications and a sequence by visibility — what customers see first is changed first",
      "A design system with typography, colours, imagery and grids that can be applied without an agency",
      "Templates for everyday use: presentation, stationery, forms, signatures",
      "Implementation on website, brochure, packaging, signage and video",
      "Rules for tone and terminology, documented so that the company's own AI systems can follow them too"
    ] %}
    <li class="check-item reveal reveal-delay-{{ loop.index0 % 3 }}">
      <span class="check-icon"></span>
      <span>{{ item }}</span>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>

<!-- 03 — ONLY WHAT CHANGES -->
<section class="container measure section-block">
  <p class="label reveal" style="margin-bottom:1rem;">03 — Only what changes</p>
  <h2 class="display-md reveal reveal-delay-1" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;">Recognition is a value worth taking along</h2>
  <p class="body-lg reveal reveal-delay-2" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem;">Not every rollout is a fresh start. Often most of it stays and only part changes: a symbol goes, a hierarchy is reordered, an addition is made. The skill then lies in making the new visible without losing the familiar — and in not overlooking any application that still shows the old state.</p>
</section>

